  "coverage_when_sigma_depends_on_curve": {
    "claim_scope": "synthetic_split_conformal_when_sigma_depends_on_curve",
    "nominal_coverage": 0.9,
    "theory": "Given exchangeable scenes, split conformal on scores |y-hat(x; curve_A)| / sigma_raw(x; curve_A) computed on B, independent of test C, yields marginal coverage at least 1-alpha on C conditional on A. Joint fit (curve and z on the same worlds) is not that split and can be optimistic. The guarantee is not conditional coverage given a scene, and it assumes the score is almost surely finite.",
